# Matt Pocock AI Skills

Use the [mattpocock/skills](https://github.com/mattpocock/skills) set for real engineering work (alignment, design, TDD), not vibe coding.

## Project-local install (not global)

- Skills install **into the current project**: `.agents/skills/` (Cursor) and `.claude/skills/` (Claude Code). Not `~/.cursor/skills/` / user-global.
- `init-ai` (core) and `bash scripts/install-matt-pocock-skills.sh` both install **project-scoped** (no `-g`).
- If `setup-matt-pocock-skills` is missing, run the install script from the project root.
- If `docs/agents/` is missing, run `/setup-matt-pocock-skills` **once** per repo before other engineering skills.

## Recommended feature workflow

For non-trivial features, follow this order (do **not** jump to code):

1. **`/setup-matt-pocock-skills`** — once per repo (issue tracker, triage labels, domain docs).
2. **`/grill-with-docs`** (preferred in a codebase) or **`/grill-me`** — one question at a time until requirements and edge cases are clear.
3. **`/to-spec`** — turn the agreed thread into a spec (business logic only; no implementation code).
4. **`/to-tickets`** — split the spec into tracer-bullet tickets (testable vertical slices) right before coding.
5. **`/implement`** — TDD per ticket; drives `/tdd` and finishes with `/code-review`. Clear context between tickets.

Periodic maintenance: **`/improve-codebase-architecture`** (scan for shallow modules → HTML report → deepen). Every few days is fine.

For hard bugs: `/diagnosing-bugs`. Unsure which skill: `/ask-matt`.

## Scope exceptions

Skip the full grill → spec → tickets loop for trivial one-liners, pure renames, docs-only edits, or when the user explicitly asks to skip planning.
